            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I really don't think this is an appropriate number.  The default for \"LOGLEVEL_QUIET\" is 4, so we're being even less logging than \"quiet\".  Can you please identify what UART console messages are especially problematic and see if we can either explicitly disable those or pick a LOGLEVEL that is closer to 7 that eliminates the noisy ones?\n\nIf we're going to do this, I don't want it to be a one-off for Catalina.  I see there is also already a commit for Harma also.  Please work with Peter to find something we can apply everywhere."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Potin Lai",
                        "email": "potin.lai@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "potinlai"
                    },
                    "message": "I change the setting to loglevel to 4, and move it the meta-facebook common layer.\n\nWe add this setting just want to supress low priority (loglevel 4-7) kernel message from UART console only, all logs still record in kernel buffer and can retrieve by dmesg command."
                }
            ],
